{"input_text": "Question: The problem I have is to calculate this term $(\complement A) \setminus (\complement B)$ when I (forexample) let $A=\left \{ a,b,c,d \right \}$ and $B=\left \{ b,c,e,g\right \}$. How do I calculate it? I've tried, but never got the right way to do from this place
\begin{equation*}
(\complement A)\setminus (\complement B)=\left \{x\in U | x\notin A \right \}\setminus\left \{x\in U | x\notin B \right \}
\end{equation*} 
